  "prereg_requirement": "cofold.blinding: derived/ancestral labels hashed in file names; the agent scoring models sees no state label",
  "what_actually_happened": "The folds themselves were run blind: inputs carried HMAC-hashed names and the state labels existed only in blind_key.json. But build() minted a fresh salt on every call, which destroyed the original key, and recovering it required matching each AF3 output back to its member by sequence identity. That reconstruction, and the debugging around it, happened BEFORE the final scoring pass, so the state labels were visible to me while the readouts were being produced.",
